   "evidence": "In the proof, `h\u03b2`, `hrep` and the `fun y \u21a6 by rw [GenLoop.fromDoubleLoop_apply, trans_reparam_apply hu hu']` argument together produce the class identity, but no exported declaration states it. `trans_reparam_apply` is `private`. The roadmap H1 quote in the description requires both `\u03c9(B)` and `2c1(B)` for `D'\u2212D=B`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Symplectic/Floer/Cap/Area.lean",
   "fix": "Add a public lemma, e.g. `IsSmoothBasedCap.rawCap_vsub_rawCap_toMul`, giving `(hu'.rawCap -\u1d65 hu.rawCap).toMul = \u27e6p\u27e7` with `p y = rectangleTrans (u \u2218 Prod.map (fun s \u21a6 1 - s) id) u' (y 0, y 1)`, together with the smoothness of that map. Derive `sphereIntegral_rawCap_vsub_rawCap` from it with `sphereIntegral_mk_of_contMDiff`. The `concatReparam*` helpers can stay private.",
   "issue": "`sphereIntegral_rawCap_vsub_rawCap` proves inline (`h\u03b2`, `hrep`, the private `trans_reparam_apply`) that `(hu'.rawCap -\u1d65 hu.rawCap).toMul` is the class of a generalized loop restricting `rectangleTrans (u \u2218 Prod.map (fun s \u21a6 1 - s) id) u'`, then immediately specializes it to `sphereIntegral`. The first Chern half of the recapping law (H1: \"\u03bc by 2c1(B)\"; https://github.com/TauCetiProject/TauCeti/pull/37485 \"feat: the clutching first Chern number of based spheres\") needs exactly this identification and would have to redo it.",
   "line": 262
  }
